Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.1 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub. The obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction (or waiver by Acquirer and Merger Sub) on or prior to the Closing Date of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties of the Company set forth in Section 4.1 shall be true and correct in all respects as of the Closing Date as though made on and as of the Closing Date, except where the failure to be so true and correct would not have a Material Adverse Effect. (ii) The representations and warranties set forth in Section 4.2 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as though made on and as of the Closing Date, except as affected by events occurring after the date of this Agreement. (iii) The fundamental representations and warranties set forth in Section 3.1 shall be accurate at a standard that accounts for any hybrid materiality thresholds, where deviations would not reasonably be expected to have an Acquirer Material Adverse Effect. (Page 58)\nAnswer:
